      "updated": 1780904845361,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HACKFLOW END-TO-END PROJECT WORKFLOW OVERVIEW\n\n1. REGISTRATION & OTP VERIFICATION:\n   - Users register on the platform. The backend generates a 6-digit OTP and dispatches a styled mail via Nodemailer.\n   - Profile configurations let users update bio, skills, socials, and verify mobile OTPs.\n\n2. EVENT & TEAM OPERATIONS:\n   - Admin creates hackathons configuring tracks, prizes, timelines, and dynamic judging criteria (with weights summing to 100%).\n   - Users explore events, register, and receive check-in QR codes. They form teams, share join codes, and recruit members.\n   - Team captains submit final deliverables (GitHub repository link, video link, pitch deck, text description).\n\n3. JUDGING ASSIGNMENT & EVALUATION:\n   - Admin uses the Operation Portal to promote users to Judges and assigns judges to events.\n   - Judges view a tracking dashboard (completed vs pending metrics) and project cards on their portal.\n   - Selecting a project opens a dynamic form mapping to the event's criteria. Sliders range 0-10, displaying a live weighted score out of 100 as they adjust. Feedback comments can be optionally written.\n   - Saving the form triggers a pre-save hook that queries event criteria weights, computes scores, and saves to the database.\n\n4. LEADERBOARD RELEASING & NOTIFICATIONS:\n   - Admin previews aggregated average scores from all judges on their private standings dashboard.\n   - Admin hits \"Publish Leaderboard\". The backend updates event status to Completed (permanently locking further grading) and retrieves registration emails.\n   - Stylized emails containing the direct leaderboard link are dispatched to all participants.\n   - Public Leaderboard displays standings with podium styling (Gold/Silver/Bronze highlights) and resource links.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 15,
      "containerId": "el_16",
      "originalText": "HACKFLOW END-TO-END PROJECT WORKFLOW OVERVIEW\n\n1. REGISTRATION & OTP VERIFICATION:\n   - Users register on the platform. The backend generates a 6-digit OTP and dispatches a styled mail via Nodemailer.\n   - Profile configurations let users update bio, skills, socials, and verify mobile OTPs.\n\n2. EVENT & TEAM OPERATIONS:\n   - Admin creates hackathons configuring tracks, prizes, timelines, and dynamic judging criteria (with weights summing to 100%).\n   - Users explore events, register, and receive check-in QR codes. They form teams, share join codes, and recruit members.\n   - Team captains submit final deliverables (GitHub repository link, video link, pitch deck, text description).\n\n3. JUDGING ASSIGNMENT & EVALUATION:\n   - Admin uses the Operation Portal to promote users to Judges and assigns judges to events.\n   - Judges view a tracking dashboard (completed vs pending metrics) and project cards on their portal.\n   - Selecting a project opens a dynamic form mapping to the event's criteria. Sliders range 0-10, displaying a live weighted score out of 100 as they adjust. Feedback comments can be optionally written.\n   - Saving the form triggers a pre-save hook that queries event criteria weights, computes scores, and saves to the database.\n\n4. LEADERBOARD RELEASING & NOTIFICATIONS:\n   - Admin previews aggregated average scores from all judges on their private standings dashboard.\n   - Admin hits \"Publish Leaderboard\". The backend updates event status to Completed (permanently locking further grading) and retrieves registration emails.\n   - Stylized emails containing the direct leaderboard link are dispatched to all participants.\n   - Public Leaderboard displays standings with podium styling (Gold/Silver/Bronze highlights) and resource links.",
      "index": "aG",
      "angle": 0,
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.6433566433566433
    }
  ],
